<section class="section">
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Agents on your machines record which application has focus and send it to
    a server you run. The dashboard turns that into time per app, per category
    and per day, without the data leaving your hardware.
  </p>

  <ul class="card-grid">
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Desktop and Android agents</h3>
        <p>A tray agent samples the focused window, and the Android app reads the system usage log, so no live sampling service is needed.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Contexts and categories</h3>
        <p>Time splits by the site in the browser or the project that is open, and regex rules sort it into categories.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Your server, your data</h3>
        <p>Privacy filters run on the device before anything is queued, and the server exposes GraphQL, read-only MCP tools and a full export.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section" id="start">
  <h2>Get started</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <pre class="code"><code>git clone https://github.com/cubicecho/eunomia &amp;&amp; cd eunomia
echo "BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=$(openssl rand -base64 32)" &gt; .env
docker compose up --build   # dashboard at http://localhost:4000</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p class="readme-link">
    Full documentation lives in the project README:
    <a href="{{ site.repo }}#readme" rel="noopener">{{ site.repo }}</a>
  </p>
</section>
